id: pm-fnx3np
title: Remove unpatched braces recursion vulnerability from file matching
description: "GHSA-vfj7-8cjw-p6xm / CVE-2026-93687: braces 3.0.3 reaches production through fast-glob 3.3.3 and micromatch 4.0.8. The mandatory complete audit rejects this tree. No patched braces version is published. Replace the glob implementation while retaining SDK linked file semantics and complete quality censuses."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 0
tags[4]: dependencies,glob,sdk,security
created_at: "2026-10-03T01:35:10.144Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-03T04:08:19.672Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-03T04:08:18.849Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-03T04:08:18.849Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: Zero full audit findings; no installed braces or micromatch path; real deeply nested input succeeds without stack overflow; brace and extglob matching retains dot files and absolute or nested relative anchoring; literal directories stay excluded; complete source census and coverage gates pass
goal: continuously enforced software supply-chain trust
objective: Remove recursive vulnerable brace expansion from production SDK matching and repository source censuses
value: Agent-supplied file patterns remain usable without a vulnerable transitive parser or changes to link identity
why_now: A newly reviewed advisory blocks the mandatory complete dependency audit during the same reviewed security delivery
parent: pm-qwoy
risk: high
confidence: high
resolution: "Removed fast-glob/micromatch/braces in favor of cooldown-eligible tinyglobby; retained file-only anchoring, dot files, braces/extglobs, and explicit recursion. Direct canonical and exact-count receipts now make the complete proof item-local."
expected_result: "No vulnerable brace dependency or recursive overflow; literal populated directories remain excluded, explicit globs retain metadata and matching behavior, and complete source coverage is exactly 100/100/100/100."
actual_result: "Direct canonical run test-local-murutkzl-pv12k5 passes 9632 tests across 763 suites with two existing native-Windows-only skips. Direct exact-count run test-local-muruuo0g-cxcqrl measures statements 66498/66498, branches 50861/50861, functions 13743/13743 and lines 63411/63411 across all 762 sources; report SHA-256 7b30b0196b6493ca17d53d9e1d0ea2ae323004bf1ab4767022091b1855560ead. The 64-case focused receipt, audits, static components and renewed real temporary/packed consumers pass. Exact-head hosted review and native Windows, then merged-main and scheduled registry evidence, still precede landing and publication."
component: sdk/linked-artifacts
dependencies[4]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
